ASoC: q6routing: disconnect the previous back end when a front end is re-routed

A front-end session has exactly one ADM copp, tracked as session->port_id, but
every "<BE> Audio Mixer MultiMediaN" switch owns its own DAPM path.  Enabling a
second back end for the same front end only moved port_id and connected the new
path; the previously selected path stayed connected and DAPM kept that back end
powered.  Reading the old switch reported 0 (get compares against port_id), and
turning the old switch off returned early because port_id no longer matched it,
so userspace could not remove the stale path at all - only a reboot cleared it.

Consequences observed on the Xiaomi Redmi Note 7 Pro (sm6150, WCD9375, mainline
7.2.10, legacy q6asm/q6afe/q6routing): after re-routing MultiMedia3 from
PRI_MI2S_RX to RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0, the playback stream blocked forever with no
kernel error (the ASM session was mapped to a copp on a port DPCM had not
started), and the speaker amplifier still powered up (the stale path).

Keep the selected mixer control in the session and disconnect it before
connecting the new one, so get/put and DAPM agree again.

Verified on the device after flashing: cross-routing MM3 no longer leaves the
speaker path powered (TAS amp stays quiet, get reports the old BE as off), and
speaker and jack both play in sequence with a clean kernel log.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c
@@ struct session_data
 	int state;
 	int port_id;
+	/* BE mixer control currently selected for this front end */
+	struct snd_kcontrol *kctl;
@@ msm_routing_put_audio_mixer
 	if (ucontrol->value.integer.value[0]) {
 		if (session->port_id == be_id)
 			return 0;
 
+		/* drop the old back end first, or DAPM keeps it powered */
+		if (session->kctl && session->kctl != kcontrol)
+			snd_soc_dapm_mixer_update_power(dapm, session->kctl, 0, update);
+
 		session->port_id = be_id;
+		session->kctl = kcontrol;
 		snd_soc_dapm_mixer_update_power(dapm, kcontrol, 1, update);
 	} else {
 		if (session->port_id == -1 || session->port_id != be_id)
 			return 0;
 
 		session->port_id = -1;
+		if (session->kctl == kcontrol)
+			session->kctl = NULL;
 		snd_soc_dapm_mixer_update_power(dapm, kcontrol, 0, update);
 	}
